==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia|hungur|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|svangr||slender, slim, thin|lang=non}}, from {{term|svangi||the groins|lang=non}}, also spelled {{term|svangr|lang=non}}.

Cognates with the Faroese {{term|svangur||hungry|lang=fo}},<ref name="blondal">{{R:Íslensk orðsifjabók 1989}}</ref> German {{term|schlank|lang=de}}, Nynorsk {{term|svang|lang=nn}},<ref name="blondal" /> Swedish dialect {{term|svånger|lang=sv}},<ref name="blondal" /> Middle Swedish {{term|svanger||slender, emaciated, very thin|lang=sv}}.<ref name="blondal" />

It went from meaning "slender" ({{term|innsveigður|lang=is}}, {{term|sveigður|lang=is}}, {{term|kviðdreginn|lang=is}}) to meaning "hungry" ({{term|magatómur|lang=is}}, {{term|soltinn|lang=is}}).<ref name="blondal" />

====Adjective====
{{is-adj-01|svöng|svangt|svengri|33=svangari|svengstur|44=svangastur}}

# [[hungry]], [[peckish]]
#: ''Ertu '''svöng'''?''
#:: Are you '''hungry'''?
#: ''Ég er mjög '''svangur'''.''
#:: I'm really '''hungry'''.
# {{obsolete|lang=is}} [[thin]], [[slender]], [[slim]]

