===Etymology 2===
A noun of the adjectival form {{term|svangur||hungry; thin|lang=is}}. Confer the {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|svangi||the groins, especially of animals|lang=non}} which was also spelled {{term|svangr||the groins, especially of animals|lang=non}}.

{{wikipedia|lang=is}}
{{wikipedia|magi|lang=is}}

====Noun====
{{is-noun|m|svangs|svangar}}

# an [[empty]] or [[hungry]] [[stomach]]; used in set phrases
#: ''Ég held að ég [[fá sér í svanginn|fái mér eitthvað í '''svanginn''']].''
#:: I think I'll get something to eat.

=====Usage notes=====
* In modern Icelandic, this word is predominantly used in the [[accusative case]] with a [[definite article]] ("[[svanginn]]") in the set phrase {{term|fá sér í svanginn|fá sér eitthvað í svanginn|to get something to eat|lang=is}}.

=====Derived terms=====
* [[fá sér í svanginn]] (to get something to eat)

